  "decision_conditions": [
    "The\r\nirregular shape and limited size of the proposed one bedroom dwelling, the need\r\nfor stairs and circulation space, and the lack of detail on a usable layout indicates\r\nthat the proposed dwelling would result in a poor standard of accommodation\r\nthat would fail to provide an acceptable standard of residential accommodation\r\nand living space to the detriment of the amenities of future occupiers. The\r\nproposals would therefore be contrary to policy D6 of the London Plan and\r\nMerton Local Plan policies D12.1, D12.3 and D12.4.",
    "The\r\nscheme provided no details of parking or a parking survey to demonstrate there\r\nis capacity in the locality to accommodate the parking shortfall and that the\r\nscheme would not adversely impact on parking, the free flow of traffic and\r\npedestrian and vehicular safety on the surrounding roads. The scheme fails to\r\ncomply with Policy T6 of the London Plan and Policy T16.1 of Merton&#39;s Local\r\nPlan 2024.",
    "In\r\nthe absence of sufficient and satisfactory cycle parking provision, the\r\ndevelopment has failed to provide sufficient secure, integrated, convenient and\r\naccessible cycle parking facilities and thus fail to promote sustainable form\r\nof transport, contrary to Policy T16.2 of Merton’s Local Plan 2024 and T5 of\r\nthe London Plan 2021.",
    "In\r\nthe absence of adequate refuse and recycling storage facilities for the\r\ndevelopment, the applicant has not demonstrated that the scheme would not\r\nadversely impact on the free flow of traffic in the locality to the detriment\r\nof highway and pedestrian safety and result in material harm to the visual\r\namenity of the area. The scheme is contrary to Policies D4, SI 7 &amp; SI 8 of\r\nthe London Plan 2021, Merton Local Plan 2024 policy D12.2, D12.3 and W14.4.",
    "By\r\nreason of the lack of an energy statement (demonstrating that the scheme would\r\nachieve a 100% improvement on Part L, Building regulations 2021), a lack of\r\ninformation to demonstrate water usage rates and a lack of information relating\r\nto ventilation or overheating, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the\r\nproposal would meet the requirement of Local Plan 2024 Policies CC2.1, CC2.2,\r\nCC2.3, CC2.4 CC2.5and CC2.6.",
    "In\r\nthe absence of a Flood Risk Assessment incorporating Sustainable Urban Drainage\r\nDesign, it has not been demonstrated the scheme would safeguard the risk of\r\nflooding in the locality. The proposal is contrary to London Plan Policy SI 13\r\nand Merton Local Plan Policies 15.7 &amp; 15.8.",
    "In\r\nthe absence of a satisfactory Air Quality Neutral Statement, the applicant has\r\nfailed to demonstrate that the development would be at minimum air quality\r\nneutral, not worsening local air quality thereby and failing to comply with\r\npolicy SI1 of the London Plan 2021."
  ],
